From: squadai-stable <noreply@local>
Date: 2026-06-26
Subject: [PATCH] aorus15 (0033) -- eGPU compute-only: skip nvidia-drm display registration

R1/R3 fix. The persistent hard freeze when the AORUS Thunderbolt eGPU is
unplugged or pushed under load was NOT an R4 gate gap (the internal GPU had
zero Xid in every documented freeze) -- it was the Wayland compositor: with
nvidia-drm.modeset=1 nvidia-drm registers a KMS device for the *headless*
eGPU, KWin (the session compositor AND the SDDM greeter) adopts it as a
display output, and hangs on a page-flip when the TB link drops -> SDDM
session down -> hard freeze (nvidia-modeset: GPU progress-wait loop +
Xid 79 name=kwin_wayland on the eGPU).

Fedora never hits this because it blacklists nvidia_drm + modeset=0 so the
eGPU is never a DRM device. We do the same thing SELECTIVELY: skip DRM/KMS
registration only for the eGPU (matched by the existing R4 predicate --
behind a Thunderbolt/USB4 controller, or device-id 0x2d04), so:
  * no compositor can ever take the eGPU as a display -> no freeze (R1/R3);
  * the internal GPU (10de:2c39 @ 01:00.0) is NOT a predicate target, keeps
    its DRM/KMS device -> external HDMI on the internal still works;
  * CUDA/nvidia-smi on the eGPU are unaffected (nvidia core char device,
    not nvidia-drm).
Reuses tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target() (EXPORT_SYMBOL, nvidia.ko, patch 0032);
nvidia-drm already loads on top of nvidia so the symbol resolves.

--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
@@ -1963,6 +1963,16 @@
 
 
 /*
+ * AORUS aorus15 (R1/R3): predicate EXPORT_SYMBOL'd by nvidia.ko (patches
+ * 0031/0032). Returns 1 for the Thunderbolt eGPU (behind a TB/USB4 controller,
+ * or device-id 0x2d04), 0 for the internal GPU. Used below to keep the eGPU
+ * compute-only (no DRM/KMS display device).
+ */
+#if defined(NV_LINUX)
+extern int tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target(struct pci_dev *pdev);
+#endif
+
+/*
  * Helper function for allocate/register DRM device for given NVIDIA GPU ID.
  */
 void nv_drm_register_drm_device(const struct NvKmsKapiGpuInfo *gpu_info)
@@ -1972,6 +1982,28 @@
     struct device *device = gpu_info->gpuInfo.os_device_ptr;
     bool bus_is_pci;
 
+    /*
+     * AORUS aorus15 (R1/R3 — kill the unplug/load hard freeze at its root):
+     * the Thunderbolt eGPU is COMPUTE-ONLY (CUDA goes through the nvidia core
+     * char device /dev/nvidiaN, not nvidia-drm). Do NOT register a DRM/KMS
+     * device for it, so no Wayland compositor (the KWin session OR the SDDM
+     * greeter) can ever adopt the headless eGPU as a display output and then
+     * hang on a page-flip when the TB link drops on unplug or under load. The
+     * internal GPU is NOT a target of the predicate, so it keeps its full DRM
+     * device and the external HDMI on 01:00.0 is unaffected. nvidia-smi/CUDA
+     * still see the eGPU (they do not depend on nvidia-drm).
+     */
+#if defined(NV_LINUX)
+    if (device != NULL && device->bus == &pci_bus_type &&
+        tb_egpu_pci_is_egpu_target(to_pci_dev(device))) {
+        NV_DRM_LOG_INFO(
+            "Skipping DRM/KMS device registration for compute-only eGPU "
+            "(NVIDIA GPU ID 0x%08x)",
+            gpu_info->gpuInfo.gpu_id);
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
+
     DRM_DEBUG(
         "Registering device for NVIDIA GPU ID 0x08%x",
         gpu_info->gpuInfo.gpu_id);
